## 0.5 ⛔ ZERO "AI-VIBE" — HUMAN-CRAFT DIRECTIVE (read first, obey always)

The output must read as **hand-crafted by a senior design studio**, not as AI-generated. A typical AI-generated site is instantly recognizable — eliminate every one of those tells. If any of the following appears, it is a bug and must be fixed:

**BANNED — the "AI-vibe" checklist (never do these):**
- No purple/indigo/violet gradients, no rainbow mesh backgrounds, no aurora blobs. The LUNA navy radial is restrained and subtle (see §2) — not a flashy gradient.
- No gradient-filled text headlines, no "shiny" gradient buttons.
- No emoji as feature icons. No lucide outline icons floating in colored circles as the default "feature card" pattern.
- No generic 3-up "feature card with icon + title + one line" grids everywhere.
- No centered hero with a giant gradient headline + two stacked buttons + scroll-down arrow — that is the #1 AI tell.
- No `rounded-2xl` / `rounded-3xl` on everything (pick one radius system; ours is `0.75rem` — use it consistently, mix square edges on data/tables/media).
- No over-used glassmorphism on every card (glass only for overlays: drawer, search, mobile sheet).
- No animated count-up stats, no auto-rotating testimonials with fade, no "🚀 Built with AI" / "Powered by AI" / "Generated with" badges.
- No Lorem Ipsum, no "Click here", no "Learn more" as link text, no marketing-speak filler ("supercharge your experience", "seamlessly revolutionize").
- No drop shadows on every element. Shadows are earned and intentional (CTA glow, elevated cards only).
- No animating everything on scroll. Motion is rare and purposeful.
- No inconsistent spacing (the 8px grid is law — every padding/margin is a multiple of 4 or 8).
- No generic AI copy tone (over-enthusiastic, adjective-heavy, exclamation marks). Copy is calm, confident, specific, in the brand voice.

**REQUIRED — human-craft tells (always do these):**
- **Editorial, asymmetrical layouts** on the home and category pages — full-bleed hero, off-grid editorial blocks, intentional negative space. Luxury feels quiet, not crowded.
- **Real typographic hierarchy** — one display serif for wordmark/headings, one sans (Inter) for body; clear scale (not all 4xl); uppercase eyebrows with 0.2em tracking; tabular-nums on every price.
- **Considered micro-interactions** — hover scale 1.02 only on real CTAs, a single ambient glow on product cards, subtle 150ms easing. Nothing more.
- **Restraint in color** — luminous blue (`#A7EBF2`) is used sparingly as an accent, never as large color blocks. Most of the canvas is the deep navy. Luxury = dark + quiet + one sharp accent.
- **Real product framing** — watches shot on a consistent dark backdrop, consistent aspect (3:4), generous padding inside the frame; the grid rhythm reads like a lookbook, not a thumbnail wall.
- **Custom, minimal iconography** — a small set of thin-line icons drawn for this brand (search, bag, account, wishlist, arrows, chevrons), 1.5px stroke, consistent weight. Not a generic icon library dump.
- **Specific, confident microcopy** — "Cash on delivery at your doorstep", "Pay now, save 10%", "Engineered in 316L steel", real shipping times, real return windows. Never vague.
- **Real states** — loading skeletons (shimmer, not spinners-everywhere), real empty states with a clear next action, real error messages, real disabled states.
- **Edge cases handled** — out-of-stock shows "Sold out" overlay not a hidden card; long titles wrap gracefully; prices align; badges never overlap content.
- **Consistency is the craft** — same border treatment, same button heights, same card padding, same focus-ring style across the entire app. Inconsistency is the loudest AI tell after the gradient hero.
- **No "demo" energy** — there is no admin teaser, no sample data that reads as fake, no placeholder products. The catalog, copy, and flows feel like a live store.

**Golden rule:** a senior designer reviewing the live site for 60 seconds should not suspect AI. When in doubt, remove, simplify, and quiet it down. Restraint reads as human; abundance reads as AI.

